#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:13 dfe0c090e68a46aa875f06ac16c54727
msgid "Appendix A — End-to-End: From Messy Folder to Published Wiki"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:15 519b0a0ebdf248519aa541d99e63eea5
msgid ""
"This appendix reproduces, step by step, the promise of Part II: turn a "
"few hand-written files into a well-formed wiki, with frontmatter, "
"classification, a trust audit, and a live HTTP server. Every command here"
" was run against the commit that ships with this book; every piece of "
"output is real, captured from a clean `/tmp` directory, not fabricated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:22 e325ad9b3ba243828c26efb9c30573a5
msgid ""
"Run it yourself in fifteen minutes, and you will have a working mental "
"model for everything Chapter 4 through Chapter 7 described."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:25 77618751f974463db4f9c9a0aa033a8c
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:27 7f68184dd2164861acd733fb0282f8e9
msgid ""
"The prose-layer chapters argued *that* a file-based, pipeline-validated "
"wiki is the right substrate for a software KB. This appendix shows the "
"argument running end-to-end, with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:31 b055823be8fd4c56bcb0761badc813c5
msgid "a deliberately small input (three files of different shapes);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:32 9b8ba03c15a44f34958db258cc51cecf
msgid "zero network dependencies (the heuristic classifier is forced on);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:33 26f91079e74a43e58eecb164d2319b44
msgid "zero hidden state (every output is a file you can `cat`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:35 9369919b2bda4a1b850632d700061bff
msgid ""
"If this walkthrough fails on your machine, something in the tooling is "
"wrong *before* any of the deeper book chapters can mean what they say. "
"Fix that first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:39 928a93c7061f4c45bfd227c4e81f1fc2
msgid "What"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:41 e4912eb1d6e34f95a8d4251f0a9d0ff2
msgid "A three-stage transcript:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:43 a128bbdfca3645288705bbf3bd498667
msgid "Prepare three input files of mixed shape (`.md`, `.txt`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:44 666752a83dc3460c968610a6204f2764
msgid ""
"Run the six CLI verbs: `init → import dir → verify → build → status → "
"serve`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:46 8217b929968f4765be00d5d3fad1a99b
msgid ""
"Observe that each stage wrote something real to disk, and that the final "
"`content/` directory is a legitimate, hand-readable wiki."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:49 641b7720dcea4480b8a0be8aafab9da3
msgid "How"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:51 4552cd73adb44c138702984a5df565f4
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:59 0e3f70d4c82240118ae6c8edfd2017f0
msgid ""
"For this appendix we disable the LLM classifier to keep the output byte-"
"identical across machines. The heuristic classifier is the fallback path "
"Chapter 6 described; it is strictly less clever than a real LLM, which "
"makes it perfect for a book."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:69 197e7e0be4ee4126960baf3326ecb979
msgid "Stage 1 — the messy input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:116 df5bbbb218bb4aa9bdf66b56b85ac277
msgid ""
"Three files, three shapes. One is a how-to (title starts with \"How "
"to\"); one is a reference (structured endpoints); one is an explanation "
"(`.txt`, no Markdown heading). A good pipeline should correctly place at "
"least the first two into their Diátaxis buckets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:121 790d1577501a48e9ad620c5712ff378d
msgid "Stage 2 — run the six verbs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:123 477d760bc1d54eb585c9c79a94a479f2
msgid ""
"**`init`** scaffolds a fresh wiki, copies the template, and creates an "
"admin account:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:146 6d0b8ac06cdc47e49f4e14a01d94e731
msgid ""
"`content/` has a few seeded pages from the template. `metadata/` has the "
"`SCHEMA.md` contract (Chapter 5), `users.yaml` with the generated admin "
"hash, and a skeleton `wiki.yaml` config. Every byte is plain text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:151 ce48892ed615450598baf58d28b77438
msgid ""
"**`import dir`** walks the input tree, classifies each file, writes a "
"page under `content/`, and logs the import:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:159 088fa6fcece34a5aaae585b2c46604bc
msgid "Three input files, three created pages. Let's inspect one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:191 da6d444ebbbc41a2857ce633549eeaa7
msgid ""
"Notice what the pipeline got *exactly right* and what it got only "
"*approximately right* — both are useful to see, because they tell you "
"where the heuristic stops helping:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:195 840d93c18df246c0bf14ff63d1763e89
msgid ""
"Right: `title` pulled from the first `# ` heading; `slug` derived from "
"the filename; `summary` snipped to the first 100 characters; "
"`source.path` recording the exact input file; `verification_status` set "
"to `unreviewed` (Chapter 5's trust default, applied even for human-"
"authored input)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:200 1c2e31296e524d63b1a1a8fafc994273
msgid ""
"Approximate: `doc_type: reference`. A real LLM classifier would have "
"picked `how-to` from the \"How to install…\" title. The heuristic does "
"not cross-check the title against the Diátaxis buckets. This is a "
"finding, not a bug: humans (or a smarter classifier, later) can promote "
"the `doc_type`, and `verify` below will flag it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:206 71770e42e6254e53a4c5467bc99dbf23
msgid "**`verify`** audits every page and emits a structured report:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:222 cf4173f701d24013abe77f0765b7b1dd
msgid ""
"Six issues, all of type `consistency`: the *template-seeded* sample pages"
" ship with slugs that do not match their filenames (e.g. a file called "
"`concurrency.md` whose slug says `go-concurrency-patterns`), which is the"
" seed author's style. None of our three imported pages triggered any "
"issue. Production use would either rename the seeds or use `verify "
"--auto-fix`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:229 b1c817f3b8ce4afab8b919bc49273783
msgid ""
"The important thing is that `verify` ran in well under a second and "
"emitted a machine-readable report. Wiring this into CI as `wiki-cli "
"verify | jq '.summary.total_issues'` and failing the build when the "
"number climbs is the obvious next step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:234 edb79bfdcb0f4cdb9ac717de4a53b40f
msgid ""
"**`build`** rebuilds the in-memory index and the INDEX.md file that feeds"
" the static-publishing path (Chapter 7):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:242 1670d5a25b2646b68063672fe2266b81
msgid "**`status`** reports the top-level health numbers as JSON:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:262 7de0c1a5b27f473193edea187815926a
msgid ""
"Ten pages (seven from the template + three we imported), no raw sources "
"pending. `git_available: false` because `/tmp/book-appx-a/wiki` is not a "
"Git repository — running `git init` inside it would flip this to `true` "
"and unlock the auto-commit behaviour described in Chapter 5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:267 4d1ef563b90c4e02996ee0932a1e5870
msgid "**`serve`** starts the HTTP server against the same tree:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:277 41e72b0a5ddd41b3a53df45b20b5a71b
msgid ""
"Visit `http://localhost:7500/pages/install` in a browser; the page from "
"`content/install.md` renders with its frontmatter hidden and the Markdown"
" body converted to HTML. Query "
"`http://localhost:7500/api/v1/search?q=port` and the tokeniser described "
"in Chapter 7 will return both the `install` page and any seeded page that"
" mentions \"port\" — because the in-memory index now has everything under"
" `content/` in its postings list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:285 225f8a3cb0fc45a2b11cf1d51bc768bc
msgid "Stage 3 — make it a Git repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:287 9488894965fa40969f5a04c9f8616d63
msgid ""
"The reason file-based wikis exist is so that everything you just built "
"can be versioned as code. Two commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:297 77ef7d3fc7854f4ea142d69a050e7188
msgid "Re-run `status` and observe:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:305 5326c6d24cb54046b72cebe0c7909b34
msgid ""
"The wiki now carries its commit SHA in the status output, and any future "
"write through the API will auto-commit with a descriptive message and "
"write the new commit SHA into the affected page's `frontmatter.commit` "
"field — the where-provenance claim of Chapter 5 becomes operational."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:311 7318844a17034e919bdfeea91473f347
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:313 955e6989186845f59cdc53663c00c5ca
msgid "A concrete artefact from this run, re-examined:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:333 c7d237340d2a4ed9a1db5fb98d01ca6f
msgid ""
"Seven of the fields encode the Chapter 5 provenance record. "
"`verification_status: unreviewed` is the trust default that survives the "
"roundtrip. `source.path` carries the exact disk location of the input. "
"None of this took a database; none of it required a vendor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:338 537134247a7743d5823821d01233beac
msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:340 aee279dd02e243cc8674d53ebc743218
msgid ""
"Part II's four chapters described the prose layer in the abstract; this "
"appendix demonstrated that the abstraction is *small enough to hold in "
"your hand*. A single binary, four commands, three input files, and "
"fifteen minutes later, you have a working, auditable, searchable, "
"publishable wiki."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:346 6083962e958645e0bb045029989d99d2
msgid "Two takeaways worth stating explicitly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:348 84cd54d1463e441ea0d36d2168d654dd
msgid ""
"**The heuristic classifier is a feature, not a weakness.** It guarantees "
"the pipeline works in air-gapped environments, makes test reproduction "
"trivial, and sets a clear performance floor that an LLM classifier has to"
" *beat* to justify its cost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:352 0a29f69b2c2d49859ef65e371b4ebd19
msgid ""
"**Every stage committed to disk.** Nothing in the walkthrough lives only "
"in memory. Turn off the server, turn off the laptop, come back tomorrow —"
" the wiki is still there in `/tmp/book-appx-a/wiki/`, still valid, still "
"reviewable in Git."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-a-example-wiki/index.md:357 f9d49d47f7f0431e82f20992bdaa5b25
msgid ""
"From here, the book moves to the code layer. Part III will take *the same"
" file-based discipline* and apply it to what the compiler knows about the"
" source tree: embeddings, a code graph, and the hybrid retrieval that "
"lets an AI assistant reason about both the prose in this appendix and the"
" code it describes."
msgstr ""

